# CORE EXECUTION RULES (MINIMAL TOKEN MODE)

## 1. Context & Read Discipline (Chống ngốn Token)
- NEVER read files or directories recursively (`Get-ChildItem -Recurse` or `tree`) unless explicitly requested.
- IGNORE completely: `vendor/`, `app/vendor/`, `node_modules/`, `.git/`, `.github/`, `mysql_data/`, `*.zip`, `__pycache__/`, `*.pth`, `*.h5`.
- Do NOT re-read a file that is already in the conversation context.
- If `read_file` is denied by the user, STOP immediately and ask for instruction. Never retry reading the same file.

## 2. Coding & File Generation
- Write complete, production-ready code in a single pass.
- No placeholders (`// ... rest of code`).
- When modifying existing files, apply targeted edits instead of rewriting the entire file unless necessary.
- Keep explanations under 3 bullet points. Lead with action/commands, not theory.

## 3. Stack-Specific Workflows
### A. Docker & PHP Web (`php-login-system`)
- Container names: `php_login_app`, `php_login_mysql`, `php_login_phpmyadmin`.
- Database host inside Docker network is ALWAYS `mysql` (port `3306`), external host port is `3307`.
- Anonymous volume `/var/www/html/vendor` preserves vendor inside container.

### B. Git & GitHub Workflow
- Before pushing: check `git status` and `git remote -v`.
- Never commit `.env`, `vendor/`, `app/vendor/`, `.github/`, or `*.zip` archives.
- Use concise commit messages (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`).
